        \u001b[36m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m│\u001b[0m \u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1;36;40moutput.wav\u001b[0m: This is the \u001b[1moutput\u001b[0m file. Because you didn't specify a \"codec\" (the method of encoding), FFmpeg looks at the file extension \u001b[36m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m│\u001b[0m \u001b[1m   \u001b[0m(\u001b[1;36;40m.wav\u001b[0m) and automatically chooses the default settings for that format (usually uncompressed 16-bit PCM audio).                         \u001b[36m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                           \u001b[36m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m│\u001b[0m \u001b[1;35m2. What happens during execution?\u001b[0m                                                                                                         \u001b[36m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                           \u001b[36m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m│\u001b[0m \u001b[36m 1 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mDecoding\u001b[0m: FFmpeg reads the \u001b[1;36;40minput.mp3\u001b[0m file and decodes the compressed MP3 data into raw, uncompressed audio frames.                     \u001b[36m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m│\u001b[0m \u001b[36m 2 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mTranscoding\u001b[0m: It takes those raw frames and prepares them for the WAV container.                                                        \u001b[36m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m│\u001b[0m \u001b[36m 3 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mEncoding\u001b[0m: It encodes the frames into the WAV format (typically PCM).                                                                   \u001b[36m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m│\u001b[0m \u001b[36m 4 \u001b[0m\u001b[1mMuxing\u001b[0m: It wraps the encoded audio into a \u001b[1;36;40m.wav\u001b[0m file structure and writes it to your disk.                                              \u001b[36m│\u001b[0m\r\n